{
  "_comment": [
    "What each creature a book wrote `tamable` is tempted and tamed with: the thing it would want, which is seldom",
    "what it drops. An item, `#` and an item tag, or `{\"item\": ..., \"potions\": [...]}` for one holding a potion;",
    "`\"babies_only\": true` for what only its young want. Held, it brings the creature and keeps it from attacking",
    "whoever holds it; given, one in three is taken. A creature not named here is not tamed this way, which leaves",
    "the ones vanilla tames (wolves, cats, parrots, horses, llamas, camels, nautiluses) to vanilla. The undead",
    "remember what they loved alive."
  ],
